  "foaf:name": "Decade Coordination Office for Tropical Americas and Caribbean",
  "sdo:name": "Decade Coordination Office for Tropical Americas and Caribbean",
  "sdo:description": "The Tropical Americas and Caribbean (TAC) Region encompasses the Western Tropical Atlantic, Caribbean Sea, and Eastern Tropical Pacific, and includes some of the most biologically rich and geopolitically diverse marine areas in the world. It is home to many Small Island Developing States (SIDS), coastal nations, and overseas territories whose economies and cultures are deeply tied to the ocean. Yet, challenges persist across the region, including fragmented marine spatial planning, weak governance in areas beyond national jurisdiction (ABNJ), limited regional ocean observation infrastructure, and persistent gaps in capacity, especially for island and coastal communities.Fisheries, aquaculture, and marine-based tourism are key pillars of the region’s economy and food security, but are under increasing threat from climate change, marine pollution, and overexploitation. Despite these pressures, there remain significant gaps in ecosystem-based management, the application of ocean science and services, and the capacity to enforce regulations that support ocean conservation and sustainable use. The TAC Decade Coordination Office plays a central role in advancing coordinated action across the region. It works in partnership with national governments, SIDS, regional organizations, academia, NGOs and the private sector to support the co-design, implementation, and monitoring of Ocean Decade Actions.",
  "sdo:location": "Colombia",
  "sdo:identifier": "UN47",
  "sdo:url": "https://oceandecade.org/actions/decade-coordination-office-for-the-tropical-americas-and-caribbean/",
